    "title": "Check Your Understanding",
    "long_instructions": "## Check Your Understanding\r\n\r\nLook at this situation:\r\n\r\nA user opens your app, but the API is down. The app tries to fetch data, but the request fails.\r\n\r\n> 1. If the code has no `try...catch`, what might the user experience?\r\n>\r\n> 2. If the code uses `try...catch` with a fallback message, how does that change the user experience?\r\n>\r\n> 3. Why does the second version make the app feel more trustworthy?",
